    "body": "Problem:\nWhen using `:tab drop` with 'splitright' enabled and a terminal split, `do_arg_all()` temporarily switches to the last window (`lastwin`), which is the terminal buffer. After creating the new tabpage, it decrements `autocmd_no_enter` and calls `goto_tabpage_tp(last_curtab, true, true)` to restore `last_curwin`. This triggers `TabEnter`, `WinEnter`, and `BufEnter` on the terminal buffer, running user autocommands such as `startinsert`. Since insert mode is global, the new tab unexpectedly starts in insert mode (#27758). This also causes spurious `TabLeave` and `TabEnter` events (#14567).\n\nSolution:\nAvoid switching to `lastwin` when `:tab` is used, and update `last_curtab->tp_curwin` directly instead of jumping back and forth between tabpages with autocommands enabled.\n\nFixes #14567\nCloses #27758",
